	<Faction id="clan_b_kimotsuki_1" is_noble="true" name="{=PKFVNkLc}Kimotsuki-shi" tier="3" owner="Hero.lord_1_uwai_6" culture="Culture.saikai" super_faction="Kingdom.shimazu" banner_key="11.205.205.1528.1528.764.764.1.0.0.1070.217.217.483.483.764.764.0.0.0"/>
	<Faction id="clan_b_saigo_1" is_noble="true" name="{=BosSaigo}Saigo-shi" tier="5" owner="Hero.lord_1_b_saigo" culture="Culture.saikai" super_faction="Kingdom.shimazu" banner_key="11.205.205.1528.1528.764.764.1.0.0.1036.217.217.483.483.764.764.0.0.0" text="{=BaDTSaig}The Saigō are not daimyō, but few wield as much influence in Satsuma as Saigō Takamori. A samurai of humble origin and towering presence, Saigō is a leading voice in the sonnō jōi movement. Beloved by the lower samurai and feared by political rivals, he walks a tightrope between personal loyalty to the Shimazu clan and his growing vision for a reformed Japan. In 1864, Saigō has returned from exile to help Satsuma crush the Chōshū rebellion, but his heart lies with imperial cause. Torn between duty and destiny, the Saigō family rises not through land or armies, but through the charisma and ideals of its reluctant champion."/>
	<Faction id="clan_b_okubo_1" is_noble="true" name="{=BosOkubo}Okubo-shi" tier="5" owner="Hero.lord_1_b_okubo" culture="Culture.saikai" super_faction="Kingdom.shimazu" banner_key="11.205.205.1528.1528.764.764.0.1.0.651.217.217.483.483.764.764.0.0.0" text="{=BaDTOkub}Hailing from a modest samurai background in Kagoshima, the Ōkubo are bureaucrats rather than warriors—but it is in politics that they sharpen their blades. Ōkubo Toshimichi, pragmatic and sharp-tongued, is fast becoming one of the most feared minds in Satsuma. A staunch ally of Saigō Takamori, he believes that only radical reform can save Japan from subjugation by the West. While others cry for war against foreign powers, Ōkubo sees the greater enemy in Japan's own corruption and feudal stagnation. As the Satsuma domain balances on the edge of rebellion, the Ōkubo clan builds networks, forges alliances, and prepares to steer the storm. In 1864, they are the hidden hand guiding the future of a crumbling shogunate."/>
